cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Yangtze-Landcover-Methane: reproduction and rework of a 2023 master's thesis on urban methane in the Yangtze River Delta"
authors:
  - family-names: Duyst
    given-names: Matthew
    # TODO: fill in once an ORCID is registered.
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/matt-duyst/Yangtze-Landcover-Methane"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  This repository holds a reproduction and reworking of a 2023 Master of
  Environmental Science thesis on forecasting historical atmospheric methane
  concentrations over China's Yangtze River Delta from urban and paddied rice
  extents. It contains the original analysis as submitted alongside a rebuilt
  pipeline, so that the two can be compared directly. ERRATA.md documents
  defects found in the original work during that reproduction.
references:
  - type: thesis
    thesis-type: "Master of Environmental Science thesis"
    title: "Urban-Methane Transfers (2000 - 2018): A Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) Approach at Forecasting Historical XCH4 Emissions through Urban Boundaries and Paddied Rice Extents Along China's YRD"
    authors:
      - family-names: Duyst
        given-names: Matthew
    institution:
      name: "Yale School of the Environment"
    year: 2023
    month: 4
    notes: "Advisor: Xuhui Lee. CFF 1.2.0 defines no advisor or supervisor field for a reference, so the role is recorded here rather than in an invented key."
